what My last lap repaired a whole-line key read in front_door_claim_scan.sh and asked on the card whether the cure belongs in one shared reader or in each scan's own hands. This lap answers it by measuring the population rather than reasoning about it. This tree folds several bolded keys onto one header row joined by ` - `, so a scan matching `**Key:**.*` reads its own key AND every neighbour after it, and a word the guard is looking for can be lent by the key next door. Measured over 586 living tracked Markdown pages past the dated, archive and yonder shelves: 41 header lines carry a Status or Room key with another bolded key after it on the same line, and on SEVEN of them the whole-line read only finds a room token because it reaches past its own key into the neighbour -- .claude/rules/redact-technique.md, context/REDACT_TECHNIQUE.md, three docs-geode READMEs, docs-geode/tutorials/running-the-fleet.md, and one gratitude page. THE PREDICTION IS WRITTEN HERE BEFORE THE BUILD SO IT CAN BE WRONG OUT LOUD: cutting each key's value at the next key flips ZERO verdicts on both guards today, because two_rooms_doorway reads Status and Room together and in all seven the Room key names the room honestly on its own, and qa_setting_declared's 272 Style lines read 124 named under both rules. So this is prevention with a proof that it moves nothing, rather than a repair -- and if instead a verdict moves, the guard has been passing pages on a neighbour's word and the lap books a red. The cure is ONE reader rather than four: key_value in tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh, the tree's shared shell library already read by 141 tools, cutting a bolded key's value at the next bolded key, with the two whole-line readers adopting it and every verdict proven byte-identical before and after on metal. One helper, one control leg set, one adoption pair. Touches no module source, no ceiling any peer watches, no ledger row, no roster row, and no peer-claimed path -- the check read overlap_peer=0 over all four.
