what The cold endurance run costs 4,303 seconds over 355 lap-tier guards, read from construction/standing-equipment-runs.kyri at stamp 20260917.163151, and its CPU stands at 4,197 of those seconds -- a ratio of 0.975, so the run computes for essentially every second it lasts and waits on nothing. Nothing in this tree reads WHAT it computes. Measured by hand this session rather than reasoned: one qa_report_card.sh invocation starts 43 processes in 615ms, 17 of them awk, and three mid-weight lap-tier scans start 5,837, 2,728 and 7,020 processes against 61, 63 and 75 wall seconds -- 78 new programs a second. At this host's measured startup costs (awk 5.61ms, grep 4.96ms, sed 4.22ms, bare fork 1.96ms, thirty runs each) that is roughly 35 percent of those three guards spent on programs loading themselves rather than reading anything. The tree meters its own ASCII, its prose register, its commit bodies and its exec bits, and holds NO reading of its own proving harness's process fan-out. THE PREDICTION IS WRITTEN HERE BEFORE THE RUN SO IT CAN BE WRONG OUT LOUD: over a bounded sample of lap-tier guards the median startup share lands between 150 and 500 per mille, no guard reads zero, and the spread across guards exceeds threefold -- borrowed_number read 19 percent beside two neighbours above 40, which is the one reading that makes a three-guard extrapolation untrustworthy and the whole reason to measure the population. If instead the median lands under 100 per mille, my three-guard sample was unrepresentative and this session's performance reading is corrected out loud. The instrument CALIBRATES ON THE HOST each run rather than baking my numbers in, timing the tools a scan actually reaches, then counts execve per sampled scan under strace and reads that guard's wall seconds from the run card. It REPORTS AND GATES NOTHING: a ceiling over a population nobody has measured is a number invented rather than read, and the first honest act is the census. Bounded sample, bounded per-trace timeout, refusing by name when strace or the run card is absent rather than defaulting. One scan, one control, one witness, one roster row at tier cadence -- the reading is expensive and belongs on the slow clock. Touches no module source, no ledger row, no ceiling any peer watches, and no peer-claimed path; the check read overlap_peer=0 over all four, and the live claim on standing_equipment_run.sh edits the runner where this only READS the card it writes.
